<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Hanover</h1><p class="st-meta">1814 CE – 1866 CE · capital Hanover</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">North German kingdom tied to the British crown until 1837, then ruled by its own kings until Prussia annexed it in 1866.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> raised the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/electorate-of-hanover">Electorate of Hanover</a> to a kingdom in 1814, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a> as king, and enlarged it with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-frisia">East Frisia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hildesheim">Hildesheim</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-lingen">Lingen</a>. It continued in personal union with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a> under George III, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iv-of-the-united-kingdom">George IV</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-iv-of-the-united-kingdom">William IV</a>, governed by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-victoria">Victoria</a> became British queen in 1837, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salic-law">Salic law</a> excluded her and her uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-augustus-king-of-hanover">Ernest Augustus</a> became King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a>. He revoked the liberal constitution of 1833, and seven <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gottingen">Göttingen</a> professors who protested, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brothers-grimm">Grimm brothers</a>, were dismissed. The kingdom was largely agrarian, though railways and the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harburg-hamburg">Harburg</a> developed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-v-of-hanover">George V</a>, blind from youth, became king in 1851.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-v-of-hanover">George V</a> sided with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in 1866. His army won at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-langensalza-1866">Langensalza</a> but surrendered two days later. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> annexed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanover">Hanover</a> as a province, and the Guelph party long campaigned for restoration.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-hanover.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Hanover" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Oren neu dag · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Hanover_(1692).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1814 CE – 1866 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hanover</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>George III, Ernest Augustus, George V</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Low German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Königreich Hannover</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1840&amp;focus=kingdom-of-hanover" aria-label="Kingdom of Hanover on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4899 370 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Hanover lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5219 626L4997 651M5219 626L5219 626M5219 626L5199 691M5219 626L5300 622M5219 626L5211 592"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M5219 626h0M5199 691h0M5300 622h0M5211 592h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5219 626h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5219 626h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Hanover. <a href="/atlas?year=1840&amp;focus=kingdom-of-hanover">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption>